35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Whoa, seventy percent of our costs are fixed! Hall hire and insurance don’t care if we show up. That’s a lot of dead weight.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I found something interesting. When we charged for summer outings, weekday turnout dropped by a third. People stopped feeling those evenings were theirs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,I checked the sheets. A quarter of us do two-thirds of the work. And the same nine people set up and lock up. It’s not fair.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The treasurer’s logs are brutal. Chasing individual payments takes six hours a month. A yearly collection takes one. That’s a huge difference.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The taster forms are clear. People don’t want to commit to a whole year at once. And the quiet members feel uneasy about the cost per visit.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, so if we charge per event, the admin nightmare gets worse?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, yes. And it kills the community feel. The weekday drop proves it.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Toshio, so a flat fee is the only way to keep the admin low? But then the non-attendees are subsidizing the regulars.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, it’s a trade-off. Low admin vs. fairness. But six hours a month is unsustainable for the next treasurer.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, what if we have a base fee, but keep it low? And maybe a small charge for big events?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"A base fee covers the fixed costs. That makes sense. But if we charge for events, we’re back to the admin problem.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I’m worried about the social cost. If people have to weigh up every evening, they’ll stop coming.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I hate that the same nine people are doing everything. But if we charge per event, they’ll just stop doing the setup.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The mid-year joiners needed hand-worked calculations. That’s a pain. A flat fee avoids that.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,The taster forms say people don’t want a whole year commitment. But a flat fee is a whole year commitment.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I think we need to balance the fixed costs with the social feel. A flat fee is simplest, but maybe too rigid.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I lean towards a flat fee. It preserves the sense of belonging. The hesitation is about the social pressure, not the money.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,I’m still angry about the imbalance. But I see the admin point. Maybe we can address the work distribution separately?,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I agree with Jonathan. The admin burden of activity-based charging is too high. A flat fee is the only sustainable option.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I’m torn. The taster forms are a warning. But if we don’t have a clear structure, people will drift away.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
