60,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option A seems the most stable. It covers the fixed costs without the admin headache.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I support A. It keeps the evenings feeling like they belong to everyone. No hesitation.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,I’m not happy with A. It ignores the imbalance. But C is worse for the admin. B might be a compromise?,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,B is complicated. The minute books show friction with named grades. I think A is the safest bet.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,B might help the newcomers. They can choose a lower level. But it makes the structure very visible.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Takumi, B might create the same friction as the old grades. I don’t want to go back to that.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Kenji, B makes the differences in participation very clear. That might hurt the sense of community.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, I hear you. But A feels like a cop-out. We’re just hiding the problem.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the problem is the work distribution, not the fee. We can fix the rota separately.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I think A is the best for keeping the door open. It’s simple and invisible.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,I’m voting A. It’s the only one that doesn’t break the admin or the social feel.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I’m voting A. It preserves the quiet kindness of the club.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I’m voting B. I want to see if we can make the participation levels fairer.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I’m voting A. The admin burden of C is too high, and B is too risky.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I’m voting A. It’s the least disruptive. We can address the other issues later.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"Okay, let’s vote. I hope we can move forward with A.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,Agreed. Let’s keep it simple.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I’m still not convinced, but I’ll go with the majority.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,A is the pragmatic choice. Let’s go with it.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,A it is. Let’s hope it works.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
